  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical uniform planet is rotating about its axis. The velocity of a point on its equator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Due to the rotation of the planet about its axis, the acceleration due to gravity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> at equator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> at poles. What is the escape velocity (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) of a particle on the planet&nbsp;from the pole of the planet?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>e</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>p</mtext></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> &nbsp;&nbsp;...(1)<br /><br />The escape velocity,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>e</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msqrt></math> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;...(2)<br /><br />From (1) and (2)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>e</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>e</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
